check 1
# Typed chat in a single-player game: the 1.14d client itself sends C->S 0x14
# (overhead, a line that starts with '!') and 0x15 (chat): Enter opens the
# chat line, the text is typed, Enter sends. The injected form
# (gen-nets2c-overhead, `send hex 14 ...`) never shows 0x14 on the 1.14d
# packets channel, because an injected message does not pass the client's
# send hook. Answers pc1-data.md Step 4 [rc-link-2] (net.c2s 0x14).
# Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md §3 (input), specs/ui/messages.md.
name net-chat-typed-ama
save ScnAma --class ama --expansion
seed 1234
ticks 110
seconds 300
channels packets
input orig frame 30; key ENTER; frame 36; text !hi; frame 44; key ENTER; frame 60; key ENTER; frame 66; text yo; frame 74; key ENTER
